A||N||4||Iron Duke Wellingsley||Rebuilt engine idles poorly . . .Camshaft inspection||||5||
Z||000000||Iron Duke Wellingsley||06-15-2001||04:22 AM||||My Iron Duke has just been rebuilt.  Now, the vacuum varies at idle from 15 to 20" and it is about 15" when the automatic tranny is in drive.  It seems like it will stall and it always wanders (idle is never stable).<P>Two of the spark plugs show carbon build up after only 300 miles of driving (#1 and #3).  The other two look "almost new."  The compression is 160-165 psi in all four cylinders.  <P>The engine makes more vacuum above 1200 rpm, but there is a noticeable missfire at all rpms.  There are no codes stored in the ECM (except 12).  <P>I have followed the diagnostics in the factory service manual.  It suggests that the problem is either valve timing or a worn camshaft.  I am using a Compu Cams camshaft and Dyna Gear timing gears.  I called both companies and they assured me that timing should be right on.  Neither company had any suggestions for adjusting timing if it is not right.  I have not degreed the cam yet.<P>Judging from the way the symptoms seem to be getting worse, I think the camshaft did not break in properly and is starting to fail.<P>How can I be sure of this before I take the car apart again?  <P>Also, I have found threads in the Forum archives that describe cam replacement by pivoting the cradle rather than completely removing it.  I was thinking about pulling out the camshaft using this method.<P>Are there any easier ways to inspect the cam lobes?  Can the oil pan be removed without pulling the engine?<P>How about measuring push rod lift with a dial gauge?  Could this method reliably detect camshaft/lifter wear?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dwayne Mohr||06-15-2001||06:49 AM|||| Before you go back into the engine, you might check a few things.  What you describe sounds very close to what the symptoms Haynes has for a bad TPS or IAC. I am by no means an expert but these might be worth checking if you are not already sure they are good. Hope this helps.||||reg||5
Z||000002||fieroluke||06-15-2001||09:23 AM||||Why only #1 and #3 is what startles me.<BR>If it's an 87, have you also replaced the DIS coils?<BR>I know, #1 and #4 are one coil, and #2 and #3<BR>the other, but still worth checking.<BR>Are all ignition wires and plugs okay?<P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/th_88gt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||06-15-2001||09:42 AM||||Cam too hot for your setup? How's the power? It's probably a EFI problem.||||reg||5
Z||000004||Iron Duke Wellingsley||06-15-2001||11:38 PM||||The cam is probably too hot, or it did not break in properly.  <P>. . . will tear it down this weekend and see if the lobes 'be wasted . . .<P>Till then, smoke 'em if you got 'em<P>||||reg||1
